# Credentials never enter the submission (ground rule 08).
.env.local
.env
*.key
*.pem

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Scratch: raw ladder console logs and scratch run directories.
logs/
runs/_*

# A PyManager runtime shim that materialised in this directory. Not part of the project.
/Python/

# Editor and OS droppings. Harmless locally, but they travel inside a submission archive
# and desktop.ini in particular carries machine-specific paths.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# The screen recording and any archive built from this tree are submitted as their own
# artifacts. Committing them would put a few hundred MB of video in git history.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv
*.zip

# Written by the web app's approval gate at demo time. The gate is the deliverable; a
# particular afternoon's clicks are not. Schema is documented in README section 5.
out/approvals.jsonl

# Everything else is deliberately committed:
#   cases/         the dataset and its ground truth
#   runs/recorded/ agent trajectories -- a required deliverable
#   out/packets/   the human review packets
#   webapp/        the demo UI, served by serve.py
